{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30224 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Ambuic Acid is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its targeting of CD70 antigen, which is a surface marker on T-cells. The evidence suggests that Ambuic Acid acts as a ligand for CD70, which in turn binds to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially modulating its activity. This mechanism is supported by two distinct pathways, both of which show a direct link between Ambuic Acid and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through CD70. The presence of multiple pathways with similar scores indicates a plausible and consistent biological relationship. The mechanism involves a sequence of molecular interactions where Ambuic Acid targets CD70, which then interacts with the polycomb group proteins, suggesting a possible role in regulating gene expression. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Ambuic Acid may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact functional role.",
